<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Launch daemon definition for AeolusHelper.

  Copied into Aeolus.app/Contents/Library/LaunchDaemons/ and registered with
  SMAppService.daemon(plistName:). Shipping the daemon inside the app bundle means
  deleting the app removes the daemon with it — the main reason to prefer SMAppService
  over the legacy SMJobBless flow.

  Do NOT add SMJobBless keys here (SMAuthorizedClients in particular). Mixing the legacy
  and modern registration schemes produces registration failures whose error messages do
  not point at the cause. Client authorisation is done in code, by checking the
  connecting process's code-signing requirement — see docs/SECURITY-adjacent notes in
  SECURITY.md and epic E2.

  ## The restart policy, and why it is here now

  Six keys, and every one of them is asserted by
  Tests/AeolusUITests/LaunchDaemonPlistTests.swift as an allowlist with an exact member
  count — a seventh key fails the build before it starts a root process nobody argued for.

  KeepAlive = { SuccessfulExit = false } restarts the job "in the inverse condition":
  whenever it exits non-zero. That makes the exit code a contract. docs/SAFETY.md § 6 is
  explicit that crash coverage is *restart plus reconciliation*, uniformly, for every way
  the helper can die — including SIGKILL, a kernel panic and a power loss, which no signal
  handler could ever reach. A helper that dies while a fan is in manual leaves the SMC
  holding that mode with nothing counting a TTL; only a new process reading F<n>Md can
  notice.

  RunAtLoad = true is written explicitly even though launchd.plist(5) records that
  KeepAlive implies it. Boot-time reconciliation is too load-bearing to rest on an
  implication in a manual page (#103, decision A3): manual mode persisting across a reboot
  is a case nobody has verified cannot happen, and the fix for it is this key.

  #81 removed both keys for a reason that was correct at the time and is not any more:
  AeolusHelperMain was a scaffold that exited non-zero on purpose, so KeepAlive would have
  turned its refusal to run into a root process restarted on launchd's throttle forever
  while SMAppService.Status reported .enabled throughout. That helper is now a real daemon
  that ends in dispatchMain() and does not exit at all. ADR 0007 required these keys to
  land in the same change as unconditional startup reconciliation and never before, and
  that change is #164/#165 — a restart policy without reconciliation restarts a helper
  that then serves without checking what the SMC still holds.

  Unverified until a signing identity exists: whether SMAppService accepts either key in a
  daemon plist. ADR 0007 lists it as an assumption, and the hardware checklist carries the
  row.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.blamechris.Aeolus.Helper</string>

	<key>BundleProgram</key>
	<string>Contents/MacOS/AeolusHelper</string>

	<key>MachServices</key>
	<dict>
		<key>com.blamechris.Aeolus.Helper</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>

	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Adaptive</string>

	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<dict>
		<key>SuccessfulExit</key>
		<false/>
	</dict>

	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
